>> title: Old Cucumber and Rice Bean Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, old cucumber, rice beans, dried scallops, cantonese, old-fire soup, summer, stovetop
>> counters: The Soup Pot
>> aka: 老黃瓜赤小豆豬骨湯, lou wong gwaa cek siu dau zyu gwat tong, lo wong gwa chek siu dau jue gwat tong, old cucumber and rice bean soup, yellow cucumber pork bone soup, 老火湯, lo fo tong
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — the cucumber collapses to threads by the third hour and that is what it is there to do; leave the seedy pith in and it breaks down instead into a cloudy pot that no straining clears
>> step.1: Deep summer — 祛濕, the damp word. The cucumber is the overgrown yellow one that has been left on the vine, not a salad cucumber. It goes in with the skin on and the seeds and soft pith scooped out.
>> step.2: blanch from cold, then rinse the bones
>> step.3: soak the beans and the scallops 30 min
>> step.4: simmer 3 hr, barely a quiver
>> step.5: season at the end, never at the start
>> step.6: The broth is the dish. The solids — 湯渣, tong zaa — are spent by the end; they go on a side plate with soy sauce, or they do not.

Deep summer — 祛濕, the damp word. The cucumber is the overgrown yellow one that has been left on the vine, not a salad cucumber. It goes in with the skin on and the seeds and soft pith scooped out.

Blanch @pork neck bones{1 1/2%lb}(680 g) from cold in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) in a #soup pot{}, ~blanch{10%min} up to a rolling boil, then pour the whole lot away, rinse every bone under the tap and scrub the pot out.

Soak @rice beans{1/3%cup}(cek siu dau; the small dark red ones, not adzuki — 祛濕, which is why they are here) and @dried scallops{3}(jiu cyu; the soaking water goes in with them) in cold water, ~soak{30%min}, and rinse @aged tangerine peel{1%piece}(can pei; a pinch and not a handful — it cuts the richness, and 理氣 is the word) with them.

Simmer @&(~2)blanched bones{} with @&(~1)soaked beans and scallops{}, @old cucumber{2%lb}(900 g; lou wong gwaa — skin on, seeds and soft pith scooped out, in thick chunks) and @cold water{3%qt}(2.8 L; the pot is filled once and not topped up) in the rinsed #soup pot{}, lid ajar, ~simmer{3%hr} at a bare quiver, unstirred.

Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, at the end and never at the start.

The broth is the dish. The solids — 湯渣, tong zaa — are spent by the end; they go on a side plate with soy sauce, or they do not.
